add('Variances/covariances are population estimates in points squared. Positive covariance reduces margin variance for a given pair of team-score variances. This identity does not establish why a covariance differs. Phase 5 already showed highly correlated opposing possession counts; missing shared pace alone is not a supported explanation. No common scoring shock was added.\n')
add('## 5. Offensive/defensive calculation inspection')
add('Base shot probability is base(kind) + 0.002×(shooting−defense), with bases 0.625 inside, 0.435 midrange and 0.31 three. It is bounded to [0.02,0.98]; three-point shooters below 50 receive a separate range factor. An otherwise identical five-rating-point increase changes the unclamped base by one percentage point. The inspected 60–95 grid is smooth and monotonic for both offense and defense. It is a pure probability-function test, not a claim that a whole game changes by that amount.\n')
grid=json.load(open(P/'attribute-grid.json'))
table(['Shooter rating vs 75 defense','Inside probability','Midrange probability','Three probability'],[[r]+[f(100*next(x['probability']for x in grid if x['off']==r and x['def']==75 and x['kind']==k))+'%'for k in ['inside','mid','three']]for r in [60,65,70,75,80,85,90,95]])
add('Additional terms include contest status, IQ, physical matchup, isolation/pick-and-roll context, lineup spacing/passing, fatigue, coaching, workload and league settings. Three-point contests add a bounded defense-dependent penalty beyond the base matchup term. This is stacking of distinct modeled effects, not automatically evidence of erroneous duplicate application.\n')
add('Physical mismatches: contested height advantages can reduce the contest scale no lower than 0.8; post weight advantage contributes at most +0.035; drive size mismatch at most +0.025; recovery at most 0.012. Biography-derived attributes are applied once by a wrapper and restored after simulation. Defensive fatigue is read from the currently selected defender, preserving the earlier switch-attribution correction. Rebounding uses active units, position/build/tendency weights and league-era priors. Ball handling and passing influence several explicit possession branches; Phase 6 did not replace them with a global turnover multiplier.\n')
add('The model does have simplifications: secondary-shot defenders can remain inherited from the preceding matchup rather than a spatial reassignment; broad “open”/“contest” flags do not encode measured separation distance. These are modeling limitations, not confirmed quantitatively responsible defects in this audit.\n')
add('## 6. Controlled mechanism tests')
add('A: identical rosters/coaches/rest, neutralized home effects. B: away three-point tendency set to 95 and midrange to 10. C: away perimeter/rim/DIQ/steal/block attributes +12; additional poor-defense control −12. D: away coach defense/tactics attributes set to 95. E: away bench basketball skill attributes −15, starters unchanged. F: away endurance −25. G: away three-point skill +15. H: away rebounding +15. I: away dribbling/passing +15. J: away tempo set to 95. Attributes remain bounded to 25–99 in these test mutations. These are contextual interventions, not forecasts of an exact real player upgrade.\n')
for l in ['nba','wnba']:
 add('### '+l.upper())
 table(['Variant','N','Points/team','Mean absolute margin','Early home margin','Within 10 %','20+ %','30+ %','Paired abs-margin change [95% bootstrap]'],[[name,d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['n'],f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['points']),f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['meanAbs']),f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['early']['meanActualMargin']),f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['within10%']),f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['over20%']),f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['over30%']),f(unc[l][name]['pairedMeanAbsMarginChange'])+' ['+', '.join(f(x)for x in unc[l][name]['pairedBootstrap95'])+']']for name in ['identical','selection','defense','poor-defense','coaching','bench','fatigue','three','rebounds','handling','pace']])
add('The early home margin is signed after the first three quarters; changes are made to the away team. A stronger away defense should generally lower that value, whereas a weaker away bench should raise it. Shared seeds do not maintain identical later RNG branches after a strategic or attribute intervention. Bootstrap intervals resample 160 paired trial seeds; they do not represent a large population of independent roster designs. Multiple variants were examined without a multiplicity-adjusted discovery claim. Wide intervals and small effects must not be reported as established calibration defects.\n')
add('## 7. Shot quality versus shooting outcomes')
add('Every scoring Bernoulli draw is logged at its final probability: primary attempts, shooting-foul continuation shots, putbacks, kick-outs and free throws. Blocked attempts are recorded with zero make probability after the block has resolved. Thus the expectation is conditional on the actual block outcome and reached action history; it does not audit the block lottery itself as a make draw. Scoring draws sum exactly to each final team score. A 30-game neutral instrumentation test reproduced scores, player boxes, summary data and PBP byte-equivalently after JSON normalization. The hooks consume the original RNG draw once and add no draw.\n')
add('“Expected points” below means the sum of value×conditional probability along the realized path, not an ex-ante pregame expected score. Shooting-foul misses are included as scoring opportunities but are not official FGA. The record distinguishes those cases. For broad shot-quality categories, flags overlap and are not comprehensively attached to blocked and secondary attempts. These are modeled opportunities, not a tracking-data definition of NBA shot quality.\n')
for l in ['nba','wnba']:
 add('### '+l.upper()+' identical-roster sample')
 table(['Category','Scoring draws','Official FGA in category','Expected make %','Observed make %','Expected points/draw','Observed points/draw','Shooter skill','Defender skill','Fatigue fraction'],[[k,v['draws'],v['FGA'],f(v['expectedMake%']),f(v['actualMake%']),f(v['expectedPointsPerDraw']),f(v['pointsPerDraw']),f(v['off']),f(v['def']),f(v['fatigue'])]for k,v in d[f'{l}-identical-901']['shots'].items()])
 add('Primary pre-final-clamp probability at/beyond the 0.02/0.88 clamp: '+f(d[f'{l}-identical-901']['primaryClamp%'])+'% of recorded unblocked ordinary primary draws. This excludes the separately bounded foul branch.\n')
add('## 8. Randomness and residual variance')
add('For each scoring draw j, conditional variance is value_j²×p_j×(1−p_j). The squared home-minus-away shooting residual is compared with the sum of these conditional variances. Under the engine’s sequential independent draws, their expectations agree; finite-sample ratios need not equal one. Paths and probabilities can change after makes/misses. This is not a fixed-shot-binomial assumption and is not a test that the model matches real basketball.\n')
table(['League / variant','Early residual MSE / modeled variance','95% bootstrap interval','Early residual variance','Mean modeled variance'],[[l.upper()+' '+name,f(unc[l][name]['earlyResidualVarianceRatio']),'['+', '.join(f(x)for x in unc[l][name]['ratioBootstrap95'])+']',f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['early']['residualVariance']),f(d[f'{l}-{name}-901']['early']['meanConditionalVariance'])]for l in ['nba','wnba']for name in ['identical','defense','bench','three']])
add('No unbounded game-level shooting multiplier was found. A broad outcome distribution under identical rosters is not by itself proof of a defective RNG. Conversely, consistency with the engine’s own probabilities does not validate those probabilities or their shot-opportunity process against reality. This phase does not justify suppressing independent misses, adding correlated makes, or flattening ratings.\n')
add('## 9. Rotation-aware quality and out-of-sample attribution')
add('Reused the Phase 4 diagnostic rotation projection: anticipated minutes, active availability, stamina, derived physical attributes, offensive/defensive skill, bench share and coach context. Healthy/injured/fatigued tests pass for both leagues, including zero minutes for unavailable players, correct total court minutes, unchanged source state and no RNG consumption. Projection remains diagnostic; no hidden team bonus or production spread replacement was added.\n')
add('Retained Phase 4 coefficients are evaluated without refitting. A separate ridge model uses world seeds 301–302 for training and 303–304 for evaluation. The ridge penalty is fixed at 10 rather than selected on test results. Unseen worlds, not a random mix of games from the same roster world, define the split. Only two held-out roster worlds per league limit generalization.\n')
