add('## 12. Historical and save/load regression')
add('Thirty full-length games each in NBA 1997, NBA 2025, WNBA 1997, WNBA 2006 and WNBA 2024: 150 games passed scoring identity, period format, accumulated minutes, monotonic summary times, nonnegative statistics, shot-count bounds and legal winner checks. These are fictional-roster format tests, not historical distribution calibration. Period, shot-clock, foul and OT settings were not changed.\n')
add('A current Phase 5 career save was serialized and loaded with completed scores, boxes and summary events unchanged. Forty actual game/feat regression cases plus synthetic recognition tests passed; repeat finalization remains idempotent. Production day progression/save-load checks passed. Thirty instrumentation comparisons reproduced complete PBP, boxes and scoring. Six projection checks verified availability, fatigue, court minutes, state and RNG integrity. All Phase 1–5 production files, completed audit outputs and custom city photographs covered by the baseline hash manifest remain unchanged.\n')
add('## 13. Files added and production status')
add('No existing production gameplay JS, player schema, contract, morale, GM, schedule, city-photo or save code was modified. New developer files: phase6-instrument.cjs, phase6-diagnostic.cjs, phase6-context.cjs, phase6-analysis.py, phase6-model.py, phase6-statistics.py, phase6-compress.py, phase6-reference-efficiency.py, phase6-fetch-reference.py, phase6-notes.py, audit-phase6-season.cjs, run-phase6*.cjs, phase6-historical.cjs, test-phase6-{instrument,projection,save,feats}.cjs, verify-phase6.py and report-phase6.py.\n')
add('New records live in dev/phase6/ and dev/balance-audit/phase6-*.json. The user-facing report is docs/PHASE6-COMPETITIVENESS.md and dist/audits/phase6.{html,txt,zip}. Large raw controlled datasets are losslessly gzip-compressed for storage. No prior results are overwritten. The published change is the audit/report, not an altered engine.\n')
add('## 14. What is established, and what remains unsupported')
add('Established: the full-season efficiency-gap discrepancy is real under a consistent box estimator; separation develops across early periods; actual defense/bench quality influences simulated outcomes; the original strength estimate omits important skill/rotation information; instrumentation conserves scoring and RNG; current fixtures reproduce the published engine.\n')
add('Not established: that the independent RNG is defective; that one coefficient causes the blowout gap; that a common shooting multiplier is needed; that an apparent model improvement proves gameplay improvement; or that the limited real quarter sample identifies a league-wide causal mechanism. There is no justified accuracy/defense/ratings correction to accept on this evidence.\n')
add('Remaining gaps: complete representative quarter/PBP coverage; real quarter possession validation; matched real shot-quality/separation data; causal separation of correlated talent and tactics; broader held-out roster-world coverage; a comprehensive opponent-responsive defensive AI; and the previously disclosed Phase 5 late-game/historical limitations. The WNBA reference’s zero 40-point blowouts remains a small-sample observation, not a prohibited outcome.\n')
add('A useful next experiment would validate opportunity quality with representative real shot-location/contest data and compare genuinely matched rotation profiles over more independently generated worlds. It should use a predetermined acceptance gate for scoring and margin distributions. It should not start by reducing variance or adding a shared random shooting factor.\n')
add('## 15. Sources and reproduction')
